# Nothing here is required, and no real value belongs in this file. The app reads ONE shared settings file,
# ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), which every standalone app uses. There is no per-app .env.
# From that file this app takes ONE key and ignores the rest:
# MOCKAZ_LAB_MODE=mock            # mock is the only mode; live is refused with a message

# Per-run settings (shell environment, not the shared file; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=4850                       # Dev UI (Vite) is VITE_PORT, default 4851
# MOCKAZ_BIND=127.0.0.1           # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does)
# DATA_DIR=~/.mock-authorize      # where rules.json and worker.json (mode 600) live
